{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/794396-beat-point-when-you-got-no-xps","id":794396,"title":"Beat point when you got no XPs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-28T14:47:34-08:00","id":794396,"title":"Beat point when you got no XPs","content":"Hello again, you've been really helpful when I was asking about the investigation rules, so I'm pushing the envelope ^^ in my games, we don't play with experience points and beats: once in a while I'd give my players points to spend on their disciplines, skills or Blood potency. It helps me pacing the power leveling up over the course of the Chronicle and it's working for everybody. But the problem is: what about taking a beat ? I love the idea, you lose a social contest, you're beaten down, you failed a roll ... You take a beat and you'll play along or you'll turn a failure into a fumble. But, in the way I'm running my chronicle, I can't really do it because Beats don't mean a thing. So I'm considering two options and I'd like to have your advice on this:<br /> <br /> Option 1- Basically, by taking a beat you're taking unto yourself to make the story more interesting so I'll return the favor by giving you a Story point: points you can use to make the Story more interesting but to your advantage. A Story Point can be use to add an element to story (to modify a setting in a credible way so it will suit you), basically thanks to that point you can be a storyteller for one turn, adding something to the story as long as it's making sense.<br /> <br /> Option 2- Taking a Beat will add one die to your reserve and, at any time, you can use that reserve to improve you dice pool. It's more basic but it can work too.<br /> <br /> What do you think ? Are you also playing without experience points and have other tricks ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T15:12:31-08:00","id":794412,"title":"","content":"The suggestion for the 2e quickstarts (which are designed for one-offs, so they don't need experiences) and for NPCs in similar situations is pretty simple: instead of a beat, restore one Willpower. Plenty useful without being complicated or messing with character advancement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T15:33:00-08:00","id":794422,"title":"","content":"I thought about this but I feared that character's masks and Dirges might be underplayed as a result","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T23:39:44-08:00","id":794645,"title":"","content":"Of the ones you suggested I think &quot;Story Points&quot; are the neatest, but you might want to be careful with the scale of change. Perhaps make it scale by how many Beats they are willing to spend on an effect.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you give them Experiences as normal, but limit expenditure to very specific things (only Merits, for instance) while raising the conversion rate from Beat to Experience to 10:1. This way you can regulate the gain of the really powerful stuff, but allow them to earn more narrative powers themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T06:21:17-08:00","id":794788,"title":"","content":"I like the Story Points idea a lot, though you'll have to be careful that shyer or less experienced players don't feel embarrassed or put on the spot to use them. Might not be a problem for your table at all, but you may want to guide things by offering suggestions in the midst of play to people who seem reluctant.<br /> <br /> Much like Saibot's second suggestion, cashing in the beats for one-shot merits could be fun. Turn in three beats for one use of three-dot allies, or three-dot herd, a new blood oath, etc.<br /> <br /> If you don't like the willpower restoration, you could have it change pools in other ways: Add the rote quality to a single roll, or just do a straight up re-roll. If you have an action oriented game, spend a beat to inflict a free combat tilt on a successful hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T17:10:18-08:00","id":797083,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot, yes I do like story points too but it might be hard to balance: requiring several story points for more significant changes might tone this down. Adding rote quality, free tilt or one shot merits are good too. I may as well give a lists of things you can do with them. I'll start with those and I will let you know. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T00:17:46-08:00","id":797699,"title":"","content":"You could have Story Points act mechanically as temporary Merits. In this sense, you have pre-written mechanics that are already scaled for play - spend a single Story Point to introduce temporary Allies (mechanically, spending one Story Point is represented by Allies 1). Naturally, spending more Story Points means the Merits that are being introduced can be stronger and more varied.<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <br /> Ralph the Toreador wants to buy a swanky new suit, and despite him having Resources 2, he instead opts to spend 5 Story Points to represent Resources 5, allowing him to make a Resources 5 expenditure - within the context of the story, this is represented by his nightclub suddenly spiking in popularity and business - so now he gets to look nice just in time for that special Elysium-hosted event.<br /> <br /> The time allotted to these 'temporary' Merits will have to be defined, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}